1252 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Infographic describing six reasons for inconsistent clinical findings on the effect of non-nutritive sweeteners \(NNS\) on body weight: heterogeneous study designs, diverse populations, variability in NNS exposure, outcome measurement and reporting, confounding and effect modifiers, and biological and contextual variability. Each point includes specific examples, such as sample size, exposure types, outcome variations, dietary adjustments, and differences in individual biology. Central graphic uses icons to illustrate each point with a balance scale symbolizing inconsistency.) /K 1298 0 R /P 239 0 R /Pg 229 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1253 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Infographic outlining six research priorities for strengthening evidence on non-nutritive sweeteners and body weight in children with diabetes: randomized controlled trials, standardized exposure assessment, harmonized outcomes and measurement, comprehensive population context characterization, mechanistic and translational studies, and collaboration with data harmonization. Each priority is detailed with key action points and simple icons illustrating topics such as children, drinks, measurement tools, groups, scientific equipment, and collaboration. Circular central graphic connects to individual colored sections for each priority.) /K 1299 0 R /P 239 0 R /Pg 232 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
